<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The new sender (#14): one tick every 120 seconds. A tick proves the Gmail sign-in, settles any send in doubt against
  Sent, reads new replies and bounces, then sends at most one approved email inside the ramp, the per-company limits
  and the recipient's hours. About 70 to 100 emails a day fit at one every 4 to 9 minutes. A tick that starts while
  another still runs finds the lock held and exits 0.

  StartInterval misses ticks while the Mac sleeps, and that is safe: the next tick settles whatever was left in
  doubt and does not ramp twice.

  The sender refuses to send while the old mailer's job (com.devanshu.outreach-mail-sender) is loaded, so a missed
  step in the switch fails safe. Its store and Gmail folder are the defaults.

  Placeholders, filled by the deploy tool (#17), which also installs this: {{LIVE_CHECKOUT}} is the live checkout,
  {{LOG_PATH}} the log file. Nothing else is filled.

  Not installed by the repo, and never loaded from a worktree. #17's switch step installs it after the old sender is
  stopped and its sent mail imported. To install by hand after filling it in:
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.devanshu.outreach-sender.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.devanshu.outreach-sender</string>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>{{LIVE_CHECKOUT}}</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>{{LIVE_CHECKOUT}}/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>-m</string>
    <string>outreach.sending</string>
    <string>run</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>120</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>{{LOG_PATH}}</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>{{LOG_PATH}}</string>
</dict>
</plist>
